# Dashboard UI Design Rule

- For dashboard KPI chips/cards, keep values clean and minimal.
- Do not append inline percentage text in metric chips (example: avoid `1 (1%)`) unless user explicitly asks.
- Prefer premium MacBook-like visuals: soft glass surfaces, subtle shadows, clean spacing, and restrained accents.
- Keep typography hierarchy clear: short labels, strong value, low-noise supporting text.
- Match existing project color system; avoid random or mismatched palette choices.
- When refining dashboard design, preserve business logic and API behavior; change only presentation unless requested.
